# sitl_overlay.parm — applied ON TOP of the boat's baseline
# (params/working_crusader.params, filtered by sitl_params.py). Every line here
# is a place where the sim DIFFERS from the boat, and says why. Keep it short:
# the point of the Gazebo sim is to fly the boat's own parameters.

# --- heading: the boat runs COMPASS_USE=0 and takes yaw from a Unicore
# moving-baseline pair (GPS1_TYPE=25). SITL cannot emit Unicore's heading
# sentences, but its NMEA GPS can emit HDT, which ArduPilot's NMEA driver turns
# into GPS yaw. Same behaviour (yaw from GPS, no compass), different wire.
GPS1_TYPE 5
SIM_GPS_TYPE 5
SIM_GPS_HDG 1
EK3_SRC1_YAW 2
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0

# --- stream rates. MAVProxy's --streamrate=-1 leaves SR0_* alone, as on the
# boat, so these ARE the ROS-side rates. The baseline file says SR0_EXTRA1 4,
# but the newest real dump (QGC params/2026-09-07_crusader_ardurover463.params)
# says 10, and docs/G7_pump_bench.md asks for 30. At the baseline's 4 Hz
# /crsd/attitude ran ~3 Hz and target_tracker dropped observations as stale.
# 30, G7's value, since 2026-10-05: these rates are SIM time, and with the
# Gazebo window open on a GTX 1080 Ti the sim runs at ~0.45x, so 10 arrived at
# ~5 Hz of wall time and the fire trees' "steady" (attitude >= 8 Hz) never held:
# no docking report, no fire. Team: settle the baseline (30 per G7).
SR0_EXTRA1 30
# SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW (and RC_CHANNELS) at 10 Hz, as docs/G7_pump_bench.md asks
# the boat for. At the baseline's 4 the bridge's pump watchdog (OFF expected
# 0.3 s after a burst ends) read a stale ON after the first burst and latched
# the pump path off for the rest of the run (Task 3, 2026-10-05).
SR0_RC_CHAN 10

# --- IMU calibration, as ArduPilot's own gazebo-*.parm files do it. The gyros
# calibrate at boot while the simulated hull is still settling on the water, the
# two SITL IMUs catch different motion, and arming fails "Gyros inconsistent"
# (first run, 2026-09-29). The real Pixhawk boots on a stationary dock.
INS_GYR_CAL 0
INS_ACCOFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACCOFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACCSCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACCSCAL_Z 1.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_X 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Y 0.001
INS_ACC2OFFS_Z 0.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_X 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Y 1.001
INS_ACC2SCAL_Z 1.001

# --- safety switch: SITL has no hardware safety button.
BRD_SAFETY_DEFLT 0

# --- logs: keep SITL dataflash small and on disarm only.
LOG_DISARMED 0

# --- Task 3: the pump and the pan/tilt cannon (crusader_sim task3_world).
# THE PUMP: the boat's pump output is not configured yet (telemetry_bridge
# pump_servo_channel 0, docs/G7_pump_bench.md). The sim puts it on SERVO10 as
# G7 describes it: RCIN10 passes the pilot's switch (ch10, high = on) through,
# TRIM = OFF so a DO_REPEAT_SERVO burst ends at OFF on the autopilot's clock.
# gz_rig_up.sh gives the bridge pump_servo_channel 10 to match.
SERVO10_FUNCTION 60
SERVO10_MIN 1000
SERVO10_MAX 2000
SERVO10_TRIM 1000
# THE CANNON: SERVO11 = AUX3 pan, SERVO12 = AUX4 tilt, function 0 so
# DO_SET_SERVO may drive them - what working_crusader.params already has (the
# baseline filter does not carry SERVO9+, so they are stated here).
SERVO11_FUNCTION 0
SERVO11_MIN 1100
SERVO11_MAX 1900
SERVO11_TRIM 1500
SERVO12_FUNCTION 0
SERVO12_MIN 1100
SERVO12_MAX 1900
SERVO12_TRIM 1500
